# State Management & Concurrency Rules

Deterministic state transition logic for the SMC engine.

## Event-Driven Architecture (EDA)
- Implement the SMC engine as an event-driven architecture.
- Use in-memory data (Redis) for low-latency state management of unmitigated Order Blocks and Fair Value Gaps.

## Actor Model
- Use the **Actor Model** pattern for concurrency to prevent race conditions during multi-instrument scanning (e.g., scanning NIFTY and SENSEX simultaneously).
- Each instrument should be managed by its own isolated state handler/thread.

## Sliding Window Detection
- Use a sliding window buffer (e.g., 200 candles) for swing detection to maintain memory efficiency.
- Only re-evaluate structure on candle close ($is\_confirmed = true$).

## Resilience
- All states must be recoverable from the database/Redis in case of process restart.
- Use atomic operations for state transitions.
